<title>USA: Philip Morris Capital to sell real estate unit.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris Capital to sell real estate unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philip Morris Cos Inc's Philip Morris Capital  Corp subsidiary said on Friday it agreed to sell its Mission Viejo  Co real estate unit to J.F. Shea Co Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.  Mission Viejo Co had revenues  of $157 million in 1996.</p>
<p>Philip Morris Capital said in a news release that it sold the unit  as part of its strategy to focus on core businesses.</p>
<p>As part of the deal, Shea would acquire the Mission Viejo and Aliso  Viejo planned communities in California and the Highlands Ranch property  in Colorado.</p>
</text>
